-- title:
--   Free Fisher information of a heat-flowed tuple is at most the liminf of the normalized Fisher information of smoothed matrix microstate laws (OpenAI finite-entropy separation)
-- statement:
--   **Setting.** Let $B, N, G$ be types (in `Type`) with decidable equality, $G$ a group. `FreeTensor.Space B N G` is OpenAI's Hilbert space on the words `FreeTensor.Word B N G`, carrying semicircular operators labelled by $B$ and $N$ (`semicircularB`, `semicircularN`) and unitaries labelled by $G$ (`unitaryG`), with von Neumann algebra `FreeTensor.algebra B N G` and vacuum tracial vector `FreeTensor.tracialVector B N G` (definitions bundle `OAIQWFE000`). `FreeTensor.semicircularN i` is the semicircular operator with label $i \in N$, and for $J \subseteq N$, `FreeTensor.backgroundAlgebra J` is the subalgebra generated by the semicircular operators labelled by $B$, the unitaries labelled by $G$ and the semicircular operators labelled by $J$.
--
--   **Matrix side** (published bundle `Def_FiniteEntropySeparation` and definitions bundles of this split). `MatrixCoordinates n d` is the space of real coordinates of $n$-tuples of $d \times d$ Hermitian matrices. `diagonalMicrostates τ X R k d` is `microstates τ X R k d (1/(k+1))`: tuples with operator norms at most $R$ whose normalized trace moments of words of length at most $k$ are within $1/(k+1)$ of those of $X$. For a measure $\mu$ on $\mathbb R^m$ and $s > 0$, `smoothedDensity μ s` is the density of $\mu$ convolved with the centered Gaussian kernel `normalKernel s`. `classicalFisher μ s` $= \sum_i \int (\partial_i \rho)^2/\rho$ for $\rho = $ `smoothedDensity μ s` (with `smoothedGradient`), and `normalizedMatrixFisher μ s` $= $ `classicalFisher μ (s/d)` $/ d^3$.
--
--   **Statement.** Let $n \in \mathbb N$ and $D : \mathbb N \to \mathbb N$ with $D(k) > 0$ for all $k$ and $D(k) \to \infty$. Let $J \subseteq N$, and let $X = (X_1, \dots, X_n)$ be bounded operators on `FreeTensor.Space B N G` with every $X_i \in$ `backgroundAlgebra J` and self-adjoint. Let $R \ge 0$ with `diagonalMicrostates (tracialVector B N G) X R k (D k)` nonempty for every $k$. Let $\sigma : \mathrm{Fin}\ n \to N$ be injective with $\sigma(i) \notin J$ for every $i$. Let $\mu_k$ be probability measures on `MatrixCoordinates n (D k)` such that $\mu_k$-almost every point lies in `diagonalMicrostates (tracialVector B N G) X R k (D k)`. Then for every $s > 0$,
--   $$\mathrm{freeFisher}\bigl(\mathrm{tracialVector}\ B\ N\ G,\ X + \sqrt s\,(\mathrm{semicircularN}\ \sigma(i))_i\bigr) \;\le\; \liminf_{k \to \infty}\ \mathrm{ENNReal.ofReal}\bigl(\mathrm{normalizedMatrixFisher}(\mu_k, s)\bigr)$$
--   in $[0, \infty]$, where $X + \sqrt s(\cdot)$ is `heatTuple X (fun i => semicircularN (σ i)) s` and `freeFisher` is the free Fisher information of the published bundle.
--
--   Lean: `OAI.FiniteEntropySeparation.FreeTensor.freeFisher_le_liminf_matrixFisher`, OpenAI's theorem of that name (in `lean/OAI/Analysis/FreeEntropy/MatrixFisherLiminf.lean`). `freeFisher`, `heatTuple`, `microstates`, `MatrixCoordinates`, `hermitianMatrix` and `matrixOpNorm` come from the published bundle `Def_FiniteEntropySeparation`; `FreeTensor.Space`, `FreeTensor.algebra`, `FreeTensor.tracialVector`, `FreeTensor.semicircularN`, `FreeTensor.backgroundAlgebra`, `diagonalMicrostates`, `smoothedDensity`, `smoothedGradient` and `classicalFisher` from the definitions bundle `OAIQWFE000`, and `normalizedMatrixFisher` from `OAIQWFE002`, of this split.
-- source:
--   OpenAI, A finite-entropy separation of microstates and nonmicrostates free entropy, OpenAI Math Release, September 25, 2026, https://github.com/openai/math (result family 298; Apache License 2.0); Lean: https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/Analysis/FreeEntropy/MatrixFisherLiminf.lean (declaration OAI.FiniteEntropySeparation.FreeTensor.freeFisher_le_liminf_matrixFisher)

